#: {{ux|en|[[diffuse large B-cell lymphoma]], not otherwise specified (DLBCL, '''NOS''')}}

====Usage notes====
* {{sense|Not Otherwise Specified}} used as the last qualifier in the definition of a class or category, as a punctuation period that restricts further narrowing of that specification, such as in the [[w:UN number|UN number]] for the transportation of dangerous goods; e.g., UN1956 is defined as "Compressed Gas, N.O.S."; whether it is flammable or inert is not specified, so it could be either.

